<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Mid Wits raises yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Mid Wits raises yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	 32.5	  vs  22.0</p>
<p>    Shr pre-exceps (cts)    39.2	  vs  23.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   20.0	  vs  11.3</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    104.48	 vs  70.78</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    200.32	 vs  94.91</p>
<p>    Tax			   75.60	 vs  25.53</p>
<p>    Profit from operations 197.21	 vs  99.53</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  3.12	 vs   4.61 loss</p>
<p>Div payable Oct 11</p>
<p>on register Sept 13</p>
<p>Full name: Middle Witwatersrand (Western Areas) Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that good progress was being made at the Target gold project, the Nkomati nickel project, the Forzando coal project and in the Zambian copperbelt.</p>
<p>It said that Mid Wits would participate in a major reorganisation of the Anglovaal Group's mining interests. A separate cautionary announcement would be made on August 27, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
